{
    "name": "Traffic Light Controller (R/RY/G/Y)",
    "description": "A traffic light controller: a 2-bit synchronous counter (2 D flip-flops, with an XOR for the count logic) plus decode gates sequence three LEDs through the real European cycle RED → RED+YELLOW → GREEN → YELLOW, one state per clock period, wrapping continuously. Each lit lamp draws its model-correct current (9.26/8.61/7.92mA for the red/yellow/green diode models). In real hardware the lamps would sit behind driver transistors — here the logic drives them directly for clarity. (ngspice-validated: all 9 windows match the decode truth table exactly.)",
